// vdag.errors.wit -- Canonical HostError sentinel enum for L5
// Result<T, HostError>.
//
// The Visual-DAG host runtime returns negative i64 sentinel codes
// from every vdag:* call when the call fails. ADR-0002 makes those
// sentinels the IS-an Err encoding for stage0's Result<T,_> type;
// this file gives those sentinels symbolic names so that guest code
// can write `Result::Err(host_error::quota_exceeded)` instead of
// hand-coding `-3` everywhere.
//
// The typechecker (src/wit_load.c + src/typecheck.c) loads this enum
// at compile time and validates `host_error::<name>` references at
// every call site. The values listed here ARE the contract: changing
// a number is a release-blocking ABI break.
//
// Editing rules:
//
//   1. NEVER reuse a number. New sentinels MUST take the next lower
//      negative slot (-13, -14, ...). Visual-DAG's
//      internal/nodes/code/imports.go uses these numbers directly,
//      so a renumbering would silently miscategorise host errors as
//      a different class.
//   2. Keep the names kebab-case (WIT convention). The compiler
//      accepts both kebab-case (`quota-exceeded`) and snake_case
//      (`quota_exceeded`) at the lookup site; the canonical form
//      here is kebab.
//   3. This enum is intentionally separate from vdag.wit (the
//      interface contract). Don't merge them -- the world block in
//      vdag.wit reserves namespaces, this file defines values.

package limceron:vdag-errors;

enum host-error {
    not-found              = -1,
    permission-denied      = -2,
    quota-exceeded         = -3,
    cost-budget-exceeded   = -4,
    dml-rejected           = -5,
    sandbox-violation      = -6,
    json-field-missing     = -7,
    json-type-mismatch     = -8,
    entropy-budget-exceeded = -9,
    limceron-budget-exceeded = -10,
    network-not-allowed    = -11,
    invalid-arg            = -12,
}
